  "tour": "2011 Late Summer Tour",
  "notes": "This show featured the first Forbin&#39;s opener since November 3, 1989 (1,249 shows). Timber, Piper and Zero all contained Crosseyed teases and quotes. Tweezer contained Tweezer Reprise and the theme from <em>Close Encounters of the Third Kind </em>(aka Wild Signals) teases from Trey, and a DEG tease from Page. The Makisupa lyrics referenced Trey&#39;s favorite music (&quot;Dank Sinatra,&quot;&nbsp;&quot;Herbie Hancock,&quot;&nbsp;&quot;Nat King Bowl&#39;,&quot; Harry Chronic, Jr.,&quot; and &quot;Van Inhalin&#39;&quot;), as well as Page&#39;s House and Mike&#39;s House. Sleep was played for the first time since August 7, 2009 (105 shows). Character Zero contained a reference to Page&#39;s House. Antelope contained Crosseyed teases and a Fish&#39;s House reference. Funky Bitch and Tweezer Reprise also contained Crosseyed quotes.",
